Saltbox Lint embeds third-party syntax grammars, themes, and a WebAssembly
regular-expression engine for syntax highlighting. The release archive carries
the complete applicable notices and license texts at these paths:

- third_party/nuri/LICENSE
  Nuri's MIT license and FrostyBee copyright notice.
- third_party/nuri/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICE
  Nuri's complete dependency and embedded-resource notices, including
  Oniguruma, wazero, Go x/term and x/sys, TextMate grammars, and themes.
- highlight/assets/licenses/ansible-LICENSE
  Red Hat Ansible extension grammar license.
- highlight/assets/licenses/jinjahtml-LICENSE
  Jinja HTML grammar license.
- highlight/assets/licenses/yaml-tmbundle-README.mdown
  YAML TextMate grammar license notice.
- highlight/assets/licenses/one-dark-pro-LICENSE
  One Dark Pro theme license.
- highlight/assets/licenses/one-light-LICENSE
  Atom One Light theme license.

Source versions, commit identifiers, hashes, and local Nuri patch descriptions
are preserved in highlight/ASSETS.md, highlight/assets/SHA256SUMS.json,
highlight/assets/ansible-sha256.json, and third_party/nuri/{PATCHES.md,
provenance.lock.json,UPSTREAM-SHA256.json,FORMAT-CHANGES.json}.
